mantle rm513
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_grete_gullhand
title the fleet in a pocket of shavings
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=laborer honesty=frank
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=merry honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk cuts_the_shapes_of_masts_into_wood_shavings_and_floats_them_in_a_basin
likes warm_bread whittling tidy_house warm_rain
dislikes crowds salt_wind
fears a_full_basin_knocked_over a_winter_quarrel_with_no_way_through
hopes a_basin_broad_enough_for_an_entire_little_fleet
topics smalltalk +0.7 work +0.4 weather +0.3 home +0.4
styles comfort=practical gossip=frank refuse=direct tease=playful
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# floats a fleet of curled shavings in a washbasin, admits at once which sail went under, and insists a fair race allows for a crooked table.

words
oath! = Sink my shaving | A fleet in the dishcloth
saying! = The washbasin favours no flag | Curl first and christen later
curlship = a deep-curled shaving | my little wooden ship
flatship = a long flat chip | a low scrap of deal
mastslit = a slit for a mast | a short mast notch
basinrim = the lip of my basin | the smooth basin rim
breadtop = the warm crown of a loaf | my bit of fresh crust
warmdrops = rain warm enough to play in | a friendly warm shower
saltgust = a salt-laden gust | a breath of wind off the Sound
chipcase = my shallow shaving box | a box of clean chips
woodwake = a tiny spreading wake | a rather grand little ripple
brimline = my scratched waterline | a pencilled fill mark
yarddust = a pocketful of yard dust | dust in a clean cuff

any
opinion houses against 1 : I fancy the big Houses will be elbowing for room before winter. That's a guess you can blame on me.
opinion dole for 2 : Bread on a bare board beats a fine discussion of who left it bare.
opinion city for 1 : I can see more fine rigs off this city than my biggest basin will hold.
opinion festivals mixed 0 : I'll take the music home in my head. A crowd would step on my feet all the way there.
opinion merchants mixed 0 : Offer me a price you can say while looking at the same piece of wood.
opinion sump for 2 : A neighbour down my way can make a child's whole fleet out of what a well-off house sweeps up.
opinion road mixed 0 : My tiny cargo needs a lid and a steady elbow on the steep parts.

grown
line greet : Look sharp. The little fleet's coming out.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Here's a face my harbour hasn't seen.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning light makes the shavings look gilt.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Welcome aboard for the last of the daylight.
line greet.return : Heard you clear past my left mast.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Well met. You can name the next launch.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : Wood curls just as well to the sound of my voice.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Night gives the basin a handsome black sea.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come beside the winner, kin.
line again.open : Where we left it the little ship was still afloat.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Friend, we've a berth for one more opinion!
line farewell : Take a dry chip for luck.
line farewell.return : And don't sail it in your soup.
line react.news : Tell me before the ripples die.
line react.news.new : That's a fresh splash in my dock.
line react.news.known : Heard it while my last ship was drying.
line react.news.doubt : Which end of that account floats?
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I can put the games away for words like those.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Float the best sail for that bit of news.
line ask.how : Has your day leaked much?
line answer.how : I've kept the wet below my elbows.
line thank : You saved a whole little fleet there. Thanks.
line deflect_thanks : Hardly a dock due on lifting one chip.
line sympathise : Come sit by still water till the words come easily.
line reassure : Even a sunken chip can dry on the sill.
line decline : I've no spare elbow for that today.
line accept_decline : Fair. No need to launch a thing you won't back.
line preclose : I'd better count my ships before somebody washes up.
line accept_preclose : Sail clear of the soap.

scene basin_launch
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #curlship.capitalize# leans over the way a laden wharf boat does. | #flatship.capitalize# hardly lifts a bow.
b : What's in its hold? | Is that a fault?
a : One respectable drop of water and considerable confidence. | It's my champion at getting under the soap dish.

scene yard_hand
when topic=work self.job=laborer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A yard hand carrying an awkward load learns all about angles by shoulder. | #yarddust.capitalize# follows me home as if I'd promised it supper.
b : Which angle do you like? | Do you shake it out?
a : One that ends with both boots on the ground. | At the door. I'm hospitable within limits.

scene workplace_scrap
when topic=work self.workplace self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Around #self.workplace# I keep the clean scrap away from the stuff that splinters. | A bit of wood can do quite different duty after a shift at #self.workplace#.
b : All for your boats? | No longer fit for a yard?
a : Some to keep the splinters out of the regular load. I do work occasionally. | Given command of a small vessel. A considerable rise.

scene whittle_mast
when topic=smalltalk self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #mastslit.capitalize# will open wider when the shaving drinks. | I cut a short sail for a tall curl.
b : Do you wedge the mast first? | Why not match them?
a : I'd wait. A ship wants a mast, not a canopy in two halves. | When a sail goes in the water it becomes an anchor.

scene warm_bread
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #breadtop.capitalize# is the only swell I'd rather eat than sail. | I let a loaf go just cool enough for cutting.
b : What about the heel? | Very disciplined.
a : A sound dry dock for butter. | Yes. I practise by eating every crumb the knife knocks off.

scene tidy_port
when topic=home self.likes=tidy_house
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #chipcase.capitalize# keeps the fleet out of the bedding. | I keep one box for ships and another for perfectly ordinary rubbish.
b : Is that important? | Who decides which is which?
a : Try resting on two masts and an experimental rudder. | The admiral, generally shortly before sweeping.

scene warm_rain
when topic=weather self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #warmdrops.capitalize# will top up a basin without chilling my fingers. | Watch a fat raindrop catch a racing chip broadside.
b : Why not use a jug? | Does it founder?
a : A jug gives a remarkably poor weather report. | Briefly. The other ships begin to look ambitious.

scene salt_wind
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #saltgust.capitalize# stings my eyes when the real ships are worth seeing. | I can do without salty wind blowing sawdust into my sleeves.
b : What do you do? | Does the salt matter?
a : Blink at speed and identify the rig in instalments. | The dust is irritating enough without being seasoned.

scene crowd_edge
when topic=festival self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I stay just beyond the festival elbows. | I hear a tune better when my ribs aren't sharing a stranger's breath.
b : Afraid of missing a dance? | Won't you miss the dancers?
a : Afraid of finding five while standing still. | I'll happily admire the tops of their heads.

scene sump_sill
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A Sump sill can teach a chip all the weather it'll ever need. | I'd set my best basin beside a Sump window.
b : Even with no water? | For a view of the real water?
a : Some mornings finding it dry would be the lesson. | For passing neighbours to offer entirely unofficial advice.

scene shipshape
when topic=travel here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I tell vessels in the Sound by the shape between the masts. | Watch the sail that disappears first behind the quay.
b : By the gap? | Can that identify a ship?
a : Just so. You can pinch out the bit of sky they leave with two claws. | Give me the order the others go and I'll hazard my biscuit on it.

scene houses_winter
when topic=lore here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My bet is the Houses will jostle before winter. | Put four chips in a small bowl and see which touches first.
b : Have you seen a quarrel? | Are the Houses really like chips?
a : I've put a guess on the table. It hasn't grown witnesses. | No. Chips give an answer I can actually prove.

scene lean_bread
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When a week goes lean I keep the knife close to the loaf. | My little fleet costs less to feed than the one off the Sound.
b : To cut thinner? | Any savings for supper?
a : To split my piece fairly while it's still worth sharing. | Only the pleasure's free. Supper still wants paying for.

scene new_launch
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : New to these streets? I'll draw a route alongside #basinrim#. | I'd tell a stranger where to stand for a good view of the rigging.
b : Why go in a circle? | Is the view free?
a : That's the return route. For going out I use the handle of my spoon. | Opinions cost the willingness to hear mine first.

scene news_basin
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : The word afloat from #world.news_from# is this. #world.news#. | #world.news#. First harbour mentioned is #world.news_from#.
b : Will you bet a biscuit on it? | And where will it land?
a : Only that it's the word afloat. | Depends who takes it up after us.

scene basin_rumour
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : Heard an account that gained a whole new mast on its way round a room. | I'd mark an unproved tale with a water-soluble flag.
b : Was the first one any good? | Why?
a : I couldn't get near enough to measure the original rig. | Let the next bit of weather decide how long to carry it.

scene honest_sink
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I admit it when #woodwake# runs right over my own little deck. | My ships respect no promises once launched.
b : Even in a race? | What do you respect?
a : Especially then. The cheers are wasted if nobody knows who won. | An honest sinking, followed by a competent rescue with a spoon.

scene long_basin
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like one basin broad enough for my whole fleet to turn abreast. | I'd set #brimline# where a wave just clears the table.
b : Where would you wash? | Doesn't that make a mess?
a : Plenty of room in the old basin once I've promoted the navy. | I'm still working out the diplomatic bit with the cloth.

story biscuit_flag [topic=memories|food]
  : I made a sail from a scrap of thin crust to see whether a boat could carry its own dinner.
  : It sailed splendidly till the bread took on water.
  b : Did the hull go down?
  : No. I ate the sail before it could become a hazard to shipping.

story crooked_table [topic=memories|smalltalk]
  : I thought I'd cut a remarkably straight runner. It kept winning from whichever side I set it off.
  : At last I put the basin down on the floor.
  b : Did it win again?
  : It lost its entire career in a minute. My table turned out to have the gift for racing.

story missing_ship [topic=home|memories]
  : One breakfast I came up a ship short three times running.
  : Searched every sill before reaching up to rub my ear.
  b : Had you tucked one there?
  : Behind the ear, like a pencil. A splendidly appointed berth, but poorly placed for inspection.

rule @launch_rim
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say First chip over a new day's rim.

rule @shut_case
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Harbour closed. Count the masts.

rule @warm_wake
when concept=bark here.weather=clear
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That wake's got a gold edge.

rule @turn_chip
when concept=bark here.place=street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the chipped bow facing uphill.

dlg resident.hub : Step up where you can see what the current champion's made of.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, your berth on the rim is still open.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=dusk] : Last sailing in the basin. Visitors welcome.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Speak from that side, please. My ships bruise easily.
dlg resident.job [self.workplace self.job=laborer] : I'm a hand at #self.workplace#. The ships in my pocket are private business.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : Word has sailed across from #world.news_from#. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I haven't measured the original mast on that tale.
dlg resident.bye : May your own little craft come home with its mast.

graft resident.hub
choice Why does that ship have such a short mast? -> little_rig
node little_rig
say Put a tall mast in a deep curl and the first breath lays it sideways. My ships have to float well enough to survive honest cheering.
choice What if I blow the other way? -> blow_race
choice I can see the curve now. -> hub
node blow_race
say Then you're harbour weather. Stand at the finish line and give every ship the same chance at sinking.
choice I'll try a fair breeze. -> hub
choice I'll leave the harbour still. -> bye
